## 1. iStaffing Purpose and Boundary

iStaffing is the staffing, scheduling, clinician-patient matching, training readiness, credential readiness, and staffing automation module inside CIHH-App.

iStaffing is NOT a standalone application. It is a module within CIHH-App (Care Indeed Home Health App), which is the unified compliance and operations platform for Care Indeed Home Health.

### Module Scope

iStaffing covers:
- Clinician Profile management (supply side of staffing)
- Patient Profile management (demand side of staffing)
- Clinician-Patient Connection tracking and management
- Calendar surface for open shifts, filled shifts, pending coverage needs, and cancelled shifts
- Training readiness status tracking per clinician
- Credential readiness status tracking per clinician
- Future AI-assisted staffing support (Step 3 — planned, not implemented)
- Future AI-assisted staffing recommendations via multi-model orchestration (Step 3 — planned, not implemented)

### What iStaffing Is NOT

- iStaffing is not named "Brad," "Brad System," "Brad Platform," or any "Brad" product variant. Brad may later integrate with iStaffing as the CIHH-App compliance orchestration agent, but Brad is not the name of iStaffing or CIHH-App.
- iStaffing does not make autonomous staffing decisions. All staffing recommendations are proposal-first, subject to deterministic validation and human approval gates before any execution.
- iStaffing does not replace human clinical judgment. It supports it.

### Relationship to Brad

Brad may later integrate with iStaffing as the CIHH-App compliance orchestration agent, but Brad is not the name of iStaffing or CIHH-App. When Brad integration is added, it is described as: "Brad is the CIHH-App compliance orchestration integration." It is not described as making staffing decisions.

