## 6. Calendar Role in iStaffing

The Calendar is the iStaffing operational calendar surface for open shifts, filled shifts, pending coverage needs, cancelled shifts, and future shift filling.

### Calendar Route

The Calendar lives at `/staffing-calendar` inside CIHH-App. The existing compliance calendar at `/calendar` is a separate, unrelated surface. No iStaffing code should route to or modify `/calendar`.

### Calendar Shift States (Step 2 — Read-Only Display)

| Shift State | Display Meaning |
|-------------|----------------|
| open | Shift has no assigned clinician; coverage needed |
| filled | Shift has an assigned clinician; assignment is active |
| pending coverage | Shift is in a pending state; coverage need is unresolved |
| cancelled | Shift has been cancelled; reason should be displayed if available |

### Calendar Data Relationships

- Each open shift links to the Patient Profile who needs the visit
- Each filled shift links to both the Patient Profile and the assigned Clinician Profile
- Calendar filters by status, discipline, and date
- Calendar displays a synthetic/demo data banner during early implementation
- No create, fill, assign, edit, delete, or cancel actions appear in Step 2

