## 11. Audit, Rollback, and Notification Gating

**PLANNED FOR STEP 3 — NOT ACTIVE IN STEP 1 OR STEP 2**

### Audit Log Requirements

The iStaffing audit log is append-only and immutable. No UPDATE or DELETE operations are permitted on audit log records at the application layer.

Every significant iStaffing action must be logged:

| Event | Required Fields |
|-------|----------------|
| Profile created | entityType, entityId, all initial values, createdBy, timestamp |
| Profile updated | field changed, previous value, new value, changedBy, timestamp |
| Credential added/updated/expired | credential type, old status, new status, verifiedBy |
| Restriction added | restriction type, severity, reason, restrictedBy |
| Restriction removed | removal reason, removedBy |
| Connection status changed | old status, new status, reason, changedBy |
| Proposal created | full proposal JSON, generatedBy (model role), timestamp |
| Proposal validated | validation outcome, all 14 check results, validatedBy, timestamp |
| Proposal approved | approvedBy (with role and credentials), rationale, timestamp |
| Proposal executed | execution result, writtenTo, timestamp |
| Proposal rolled back | rollback reason, rolledBackBy, timestamp |
| Bias flag generated | affected group, deviation %, flagged metrics |
| Accommodation applied | type, clinician affected, constraint enforced |

### Rollback Requirements

Any executed proposal must be capable of rollback. Rollback requirements:
- Rollback must produce a `rolled_back` lifecycle state on the proposal
- Rollback must create an audit log entry with: original execution record, rollback reason, who initiated rollback, timestamp
- Rollback must not modify the original audit log entry (append-only; create a new entry)

### Notification Gating

- Clinician notification of an assignment is a post-execution step, not pre-execution
- Notifications are gated behind execution success
- If execution fails, notifications must not be sent
- If rollback occurs after notification, a corrective notification must be sent and logged
- Notification channels (Step 3 design): app notification, SMS, phone (recorded manually by scheduler), email

