## 12. ADS / FEHA Future-Readiness

Future AI-assisted staffing recommendations may be treated as Automated Decision System (ADS) decision-support activity under California FEHA. The system must preserve the data fields, terminology, and audit-ready structure needed for future ADS compliance, but early implementation must not perform active matching, autonomous scheduling, or production staffing decisions.

### Required Language on All Future iStaffing AI Outputs

> "AI-assisted recommendation. Assignment subject to clinical manager review and approval per 42 CFR §484 and agency policy. This tool does not make final staffing decisions."

### ADS Compliance Architecture (Step 3 Design)

**5-Layer Decision Flow:**

```
LAYER 1: HARD CONSTRAINTS (iStaffing Validator enforces — no override)
├── Credential match (§484.115)
├── License expiration check
├── Religious accommodation (FEHA)
├── ADA/disability accommodation
├── FMLA/pregnancy leave
├── Physician-ordered discipline match (§484.60)
├── Aide supervisory compliance (§484.80)
└── Maximum legal work hours (CA labor law)

LAYER 2: OPTIMIZATION (iStaffing Scheduler proposes — human reviews)
├── Distance/mileage scoring
├── Continuity preference
├── Competency match beyond minimum credential
├── Workload balancing
├── Schedule preference alignment
└── Feedback score (IF bias-audited)

LAYER 3: BIAS CHECK (Automated, before human review)
├── Run disparate impact check on proposed plan
├── Flag if any protected group receives >15% more mileage
├── Flag if weekend assignments skew by demographics
├── Flag if high-acuity assignments correlate with race/sex
└── Generate bias-check summary for reviewer

LAYER 4: HUMAN REVIEW (Qualified ACCM / Clinical Manager)
├── Reviews flagged proposals (not all — only exceptions)
├── Reviews bias-check summary
├── Documents approval rationale for flagged items
└── Signs off on final approved proposal

LAYER 5: AUDIT TRAIL (Continuous, append-only)
├── Every recommendation logged with full factor weights
├── Every approval/override logged with human rationale
├── Monthly disparate impact report generated
├── Quarterly external audit scheduled
└── Clinician appeal log maintained
```

### ADS Use/Avoid Terminology

**Use:**
- "future AI-assisted staffing recommendations"
- "future AI-assisted staffing support"
- "decision-support"
- "human approval gates"
- "validation before execution"

**Do NOT Use:**
- "automated staffing decision"
- "autonomous scheduling"
- "iStaffing automatically assigns clinicians"
- "active AI matching"
- "production scheduling automation"

