## Appendix B: Relationship Model (Text ERD)

```
CLINICIAN (1)──────(M) CREDENTIAL
    │
    ├──(M) SKILL / COMPETENCY [entityType=clinician]
    │
    ├──(M) AVAILABILITY
    │
    ├──(M) RESTRICTION [clinicianId set]
    │
    ├──(M) PREFERENCE [clinicianId set]
    │
    ├──(M) CLINICIAN_PATIENT_CONNECTION ──(M)──(1) PATIENT
    │           │                                      │
    │           │                                      ├──(M) SKILL / COMPETENCY [entityType=patient]
    │           │                                      │
    │           │                                      ├──(M) RESTRICTION [patientId set]
    │           │                                      │
    │           │                                      ├──(M) PREFERENCE [patientId set]
    │           │                                      │
    │           │                                      └──(M) SHIFT_NEED
    │           │                                                │
    │           └──────────────────────────────────────────────┤──(M) SHIFT_ASSIGNMENT
    │                                                          │          │
    └──(M) SHIFT_ASSIGNMENT ──(1)──────────────────────────────┘          │
                                                                    AUDIT_LOG
                                                              (logs all entities — append-only)
```

### Relationship Rules

1. Clinician ↔ Patient: ALWAYS through Clinician-Patient Connection. Never a direct foreign key in either profile.
2. Clinician → ShiftAssignment: A clinician can have many assignments. Each assignment links to exactly one ShiftNeed.
3. Patient → ShiftNeed: A patient generates many shift needs (one per required visit).
4. ShiftNeed → ShiftAssignment: One shift need can have at most one active assignment (but may have historical cancelled/declined assignments).
5. Credentials: Clinician-only. Patients do not have credentials.
6. Restrictions and Preferences: Can be directional (clinician→patient, patient→clinician) or general.
7. AuditLog: References any entity via entityType + entityId. No direct FK to maintain flexibility.

